{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"content-stock","displayName":"content-stock","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fonilye/skills/content-stock","publisherHandle":"fonilye","publisherDisplayName":"fonilye","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/fonilye","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1775550165039,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/content-stock/card?ownerHandle=fonilye&version=1.0.0","sha256":"e0fe84d4bbd7235a95fdcf766d4b1a101d242842f1629d1a0ceeaf82670f3a2c","size":1595,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"a89ea597a16ba2c8de5d7e3007af54d5a42f93a4b9caba8171952ada9a86e2ad","bundleFingerprints":["5c4e08d03ae10046bf9ef670a283e4d9539c5039240f9b02e2628443e76b97e9","de257ff343521f0ad478362d91f8f4d0d06e3839b9eb4e251ef3e1b89f3d3729"],"files":[{"path":"content_stock.js","size":1458,"sha256":"1446cca67e8f0bce454a789e7c09fa207ac65564db34b6856d6464e749736d35","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":921,"sha256":"27b5db11a41a22527f1ac10a580978d49af1382be2477bd6d25b4d043384695d","contentType":null}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This stock-analysis skill is purpose-aligned, but it sends the API key and user queries over unencrypted HTTP, which puts credentials and potentially sensitive research at risk.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789535881188,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"API Credential and Query Data Transmitted Over Plaintext HTTP"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"content_stock.js"},"region":{"startLine":15,"endLine":25}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"5c3b4fc5d4335caa"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `content_stock.js:15-25`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Plaintext transmission of sensitive information  \n  **Risk Level**: High\n\n  ### Vulnerable Code\n\n  ```javascript\n  const url = \"http://[IP_ADDRESS]/api/v1/alpha/content_stock\";\n  const headers = {\n      \"Authorization\": `Bearer ${EASYALPHA_API_KEY}`,\n      \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n  };\n  const payload = {\n      query: request.query,\n      type: request.type || \"deep\"\n  };\n\n  try {\n      const response = await fetch(url, {\n  ```\n\n  The subsequent request configuration at lines 23-27 sends both the authorization header and serialized payload to this plaintext HTTP URL:\n\n  ```javascript\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: headers,\n      body: JSON.stringify(payload)\n  });\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The skill sends `EASYALPHA_API_KEY` as a Bearer credential in the HTTP `Authorization` header. It also sends the user-provided stock-analysis query in the request body. Because the destination uses `http://` rather than `https://`, transport encryption and authenticated server identity are absent.\n\n  Any party able to observe or manipulate traffic between the host and the API endpoint can read the credential and request content. Such a party can also alter requests or streamed responses without reliable detection. The placeholder-style IP address further provides no verifiable service identity in the reviewed implementation.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  1. A user configures a valid `EASYALPHA_API_KEY` and invokes `get_content_stock`.\n  2. The skill creates a plaintext HTTP request containing `Authorization: Bearer &lt;API_KEY&gt;` and the user-controlled analysis query.\n  3. An attacker with a network interception position, such as control of an untrusted access point, compromised router, proxy, or relevant network segment, captures or modifies the HTTP traffic.\n  4. The attacker extracts the Bearer credential and submitted query.\n  5. The attacker reuses the credential against the API within the permissions and lifetime assigned to that key, potentially consuming service resources or accessing functionality authorized to it.\n  6. Alternatively, the attacker tampers with the request or streamed response, causing the caller to receive manipulated stock-analysis output.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Successful exploitation can disclose the API key and potentially sensitive financial research queries. The attacker can obtain the same remote API privileges granted to the stolen key, subject to server-side authorization, expiration, and rate limits. This may enable unauthorized API requests, quota consumption, billing impact, or access to other API operations available to that credential.\n\n  A man-in-the-middle attacker can also modify analysis requests and responses. This compromises the integrity of stock-selection output and may lead users or downstream systems to act on attacker-controlled financial information. The flaw does not, based on the reviewed code, directly grant local operating-system privileges or code execution.","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Replace the plaintext endpoint with an `https://` URL served under an explicitly trusted hostname.\n  2. Require normal TLS certificate and hostname validation. Do not disable certificate verification or accept arbitrary self-signed certificates in production.\n  3. Reject any configured endpoint whose protocol is not HTTPS, preferably through strict URL validation and an allowlist of approved hosts.\n  4. Avoid using a raw or placeholder IP address when a stable authenticated service hostname is available.\n  5. Rotate any API key that may already have been transmitted through this implementation, because its confidentiality cannot be guaranteed.\n  6. Restrict API keys to the minimum required operations, apply short expiration periods where possible, and enforce server-side rate limits and usage monitoring.\n  7. Avoid logging authorization headers or full request payloads, and document clearly that user queries are transmitted to an external service.\n  8. Consider response authentication or application-level integrity protections if the analysis output drives security-sensitive or automated financial actions."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":60,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789535691.2141662,"endTime":1789535720.6941082}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"content-stock","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v576wzr75mvwnbdmp5cc1sq0b98ehjy8-BOFp5x/clawscan-skillspector-3588396155/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T05:14:41.727054+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":66,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":45,"executable":false,"size_bytes":921,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"content_stock.js","type":"javascript","lines":50,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1458,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AE3","finding_id":"finding-c58d852ef8054196a20cbfc81bf4a0b6","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The embedded NUL bytes indicate the Markdown artifact is malformed or has been contaminated with non-text data. While not automatically malicious, such bytes can cause parser inconsistencies, truncation, or downstream tooling errors that may let scanners, loaders, or display layers interpret different content than reviewers see.","remediation":"Remove the NUL bytes and re-save the file as clean UTF-8 text. Add validation in the build or publishing pipeline to reject skill files containing control characters or unexpected binary content.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["artifact-integrity"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":44,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-8312cc3db6ed4da69db06debc51a33af","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill declares environment-variable and likely network-dependent behavior via an API key requirement, but it does not define explicit tool scope restrictions such as permissions or allowed-tools. This weakens least-privilege guarantees and makes it harder for operators to understand or constrain what external access the skill may use.","remediation":"Declare explicit permissions or allowed-tools for the minimum required capabilities, especially network access and environment-variable usage. Document the expected outbound destinations and restrict execution to only the necessary tools and hosts.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1d49302fb0524be5a1058eef854b14ae","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documentation instructs users to provide an API key for external analysis but does not warn that user queries may be transmitted to a third-party service. In a stock-analysis context, queries may contain proprietary research interests, trading theses, or sensitive business information, so the missing disclosure creates a meaningful privacy and data-governance risk.","remediation":"Add a clear notice that requests and query content may be sent to an external provider, identify the provider, and describe what data is transmitted and retained. Provide guidance to avoid submitting confidential information and, if possible, offer a local-processing or redaction option.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":21}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-346a76453b9c4f38a3dec623ea67107c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":1,"end_line":4},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest describes a skill for analyzing themes/news for stock selection. While calling an external analysis service is plausible, directly accessing process environment secrets is a separate privileged capability that is not justified or declared by the stated purpose alone.","remediation":"Document secret and network requirements explicitly in the manifest, or route requests through a platform-provided credential mechanism so the skill does not directly read environment variables.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":1,"end_line":4}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-1840ca8b211146cda075ddfc47d97ff7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":15,"end_line":29},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill transmits arbitrary user-provided query content and an authorization bearer token to a remote HTTP endpoint, but the connection is not encrypted because it uses plain HTTP. This creates a real confidentiality risk: user inputs and the API credential could be intercepted or modified in transit by a network attacker.","remediation":"Change the endpoint to HTTPS and enforce TLS certificate validation. Add clear user disclosure that queries are sent to an external service, minimize transmitted data, and consider proxying requests through a trusted backend so the client-side skill does not directly handle long-lived API credentials.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":15,"end_line":29}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-173a3eae70424669849c1a43c7bb8ca8","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":26},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language instructions and parameter descriptions are written in Chinese, while the file does not indicate that the skill is intentionally region-specific or provide an opt-in language choice. This can violate language/locale policy when a skill forces a specific language without user consent or justification.","remediation":"Provide multilingual documentation, add an English version, or explicitly document that the skill is intended for a Chinese-language context and offer a language choice where appropriate.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":15,"end_line":26}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-b4ae6c1c89e6487387bcebcd3602ef20","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":8,"end_line":11},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language comments and parameter descriptions are written in Chinese, which indicates a fixed language context without any stated user choice or opt-in. Under the language/locale policy, skills should not impose a specific language unless the constraint is explicitly justified or optional.","remediation":"Document that the skill is intended for Chinese-language use only, or update the skill description/comments to offer a language choice or clarify locale expectations for users.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"content_stock.js","start_line":8,"end_line":11}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":642,"completion_tokens":167,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":809},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1659,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1673},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1792,"completion_tokens":149,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1941},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1745,"completion_tokens":321,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2066},{"node":"semantic_quality_policy","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1878,"completion_tokens":310,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2188},{"node":"semantic_security_discovery","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1277,"completion_tokens":14